sing multifamily, retail, office, industrial, single-tenant net lease, seniors housing, self-storage, hospitality, medical office, and manufactured housing, as well as capital markets/financing. It also operates as a financial intermediary that provides commercial real estate capital markets solutions, including senior debt, mezzanine debt, joint venture, preferred equity, and securitization services, as well as loan sales and due diligence services to commercial real estate owners, developers, and investors. In addition, the company offers a way to buy and sell commercial property as a complement to its traditional property marketing channels. Further, it provides advisory and consulting services, which include opinions of value, operating and financial performance benchmarking analysis, specific asset buy-sell strategies, market and submarket analysis and ranking, portfolio strategies by property type, market strategy, development and redevelopment feasibility studies, and other services; and leasing services for tenants and/or landlords in connection with commercial real estate leases. Marcus & Millichap, Inc. was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in Calabasas, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Hessam  Nadji | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 854 people. Revenue per employee of $884K ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $69K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $28K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Marcus & Millichap, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $936M market cap on $755M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -17% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $59M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -17.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 57% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5720866079432144},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 24% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in MMI Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/149/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_MMI_Response_111226011601_1794507361.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794507361.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MMI Q3 2026 deep dive: market volatility and strategic investments shape outlook","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/mmi-q3-2026-deep-dive-055736575.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794376656.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"What Marcus & Millichap (MMI) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/what-marcus-millichap-mmi-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794305558.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Metro Mining (ASX:MMI) Back on Track After Its September Setback?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/metal-and-mining/is-metro-mining-asxmmi-back-on-track-after-its-september-setback","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794249420.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Marcus & Millichap: Industrial Vacancy Falls to 7.